    "created_at": "2026-11-24T18:15:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T18:15:46Z",
    "body": "Add **SF32** to the list. Description from @qsmits (2026-11-24): SF32 is the Fehlmann holder system. It is a 30 taper with no flange. It has a groove in the taper and a drive dog on the end. qsmits uses it on a Fehlmann Picomax 55.\n\nTo draw a conservative outline, these numbers are necessary:\n\n- the taper gauge diameter, the taper length and the taper angle;\n- the position and size of the groove;\n- the drive dog size and its position;\n- the length from the spindle face to the tool bore, and the bore or collet types that are available.\n\nUse only a published Fehlmann drawing or catalogue page, or measurements of your own holder. Do not use a vendor CAD model. @qsmits, if you can share such a drawing reference or your measurements, add them here.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
