    "created_at": "2026-11-24T22:37:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T22:37:53Z",
    "body": "Add these modular (polygon and face-contact) interfaces to the list. They are not common on hobby machines, but they are used on lathes, mill-turn machines and larger mills:\n\n- **KM** (Kennametal): ISO 26622.\n- **Capto** (Sandvik Coromant): ISO 26623.\n- **KM4X / KMX** (Kennametal): we do not know of an ISO standard for it. Use Kennametal's published catalogue dimension tables only.\n\nUse the same rules as the other holders: take the numbers from the standard's dimension tables or the maker's published catalogue tables, record each source in the decision file, draw a conservative outline, and do not use a vendor CAD model. These interfaces also apply to turning holders (`lathe_holder.rs`), so check the shape that U6 (#3897) uses for both mill and lathe holders.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
